## What this fork changes

- The skill is renamed `bang-motion` → `bits-bang-motion` in `SKILL.md`, both
  plugin manifests, and the documented install paths.
- Author, homepage and repository metadata point at this repository.
- Two starter document titles read "BITS Bang Motion"; starter file comments
  credit the original as `Original:` and this fork as `Adapted for`.
- `upstream` is kept as a second git remote so `git diff upstream/main` still
  shows the full delta against the original.

## Fork additions (not from upstream)

- `references/voiceover.md` — the narrated-video path: script, TTS, word
  timing, `?ratio=9x16`, audio muxing.
- `scripts/tts-gemini.py`, `scripts/asr-words.py`, `scripts/make-cues.mjs` —
  new tools for that path.
- Every starter reads `?ratio=9x16`, takes `DUR` from `CUES.dur`, and centres
  the camera on `W/2, H/2`. `starter-explainer-jurnalisme.html` also carries
  `saySync` as a worked example.
- `scripts/export-frames.mjs` takes `WIDTH`/`HEIGHT`; `snap.mjs` and
  `export-frames.mjs` pass `--no-sandbox` so Chrome starts as root.

Everything else — references, style rules, the workflow, the remaining
assets — is as upstream published it at v1.19.0.